# Teaching readiness — Creación Digital I–II (UEM)

**Re-audited 2026-08-28.** This file distinguishes a complete lesson scaffold from delivery sign-off, evidence maturity, research permission, public-exhibition permission, and generated-asset operations.

## 0. Current verdict

**Curriculum scaffold: complete.** CD I has 9 units and CD II has 6. All 15 exist in English and Spanish with B1/B2/B3, definition of done, assessment mapping, hand-in package, master idea, field lens, semantic graphic, outcome illustration, and private instructor answer sketches.

**Teaching: ready for instructor dry-run, not yet institutionally released.** The official presencial totals remain 150 h per course; the curriculum allocates 80/80 contact hours as pedagogical slices. Actual dates, groups, submission channels, room/software conditions, and Campus Virtual procedures remain external.

**Research data: blocked.** Consent C/S is drafted but has no DPO approval and has not been administered.

**Public exhibition: blocked by default.** A student piece needs the applicable signed S1/S2 permission. Course completion never implies exhibition or research consent.

**Evidence gaps: bounded, not hidden.** A gap in direct teaching research does not make a lesson unusable. It means the lesson remains a declared pilot and must not claim a validated learning effect.

