## 2. Work queue — do in this order

### P0 — before the first class

- [ ] **Instructor sign-off:** read each track once as a sequence, then mark any unit you do not intend to teach this year. Do not silently leave a published unit in the assessed sequence.
- [ ] **Institutional delivery data:** enter real dates, groups, submission channels, assessment deadlines, recovery procedure, and Campus Virtual links in the institutional system. Do not invent them in this repository.
- [ ] **Assessment cross-check:** compare each B1/B2/B3 allocation and hand-in package with the final institutional evaluation table. Record any approved local adaptation before students begin.
- [ ] **Software and access dry-run:** test the actual lab machines/accounts for image, 3D, video, portfolio, avatar, and AR units. Record a no-cost or lower-spec fallback for every required tool.
- [ ] **Accessibility route:** verify keyboard access, captions/transcripts, contrast, reduced-motion alternatives, export formats, and a non-AR/non-immersive path where relevant.
- [ ] **First-session rehearsal:** run the opening lesson against its real time allocation. Confirm that B3 remains individually attributable.
- [ ] **Release checkpoint:** commit/deploy the selected version and inspect the public track plus one lesson in each language. A passing local build is not itself a live release.

**P0 definition of done:** a student can identify where to go, what to install or use, what to submit, when to submit it, how it is assessed, and what accessible fallback exists.

### P1 — teaching-pack polish

- [ ] Before any visual reforge, run `npm run generate:lesson-covers` only from a clean intentional state and inspect `digital-creativity-pedagogy/archives/lesson-covers/<timestamp>/` so the previous generated set remains recoverable without publishing the archive.
- [x] Formula-backed track-orientation backgrounds regenerate with `npm run generate:pass-track-art`; image bytes are immutable and content-addressed, each release is retained in the public index, superseded mutable assets/indexes are archived under `digital-creativity-pedagogy/archives/fractal-pass-track/<timestamp>/`, and private receipts retain tool versions, hashes, and Git commits where available.
- [ ] Build and rehearse the Ahmes Formula Evidence Lifecycle (12H.FC0–FC4) before enabling broad design-bibliography ingestion. Keep unattended promotion forbidden; only reviewed `EXACT` or `USABLE_WITH_REPAIR` rows may enter glossary exports or fractal-architect briefs.
- [ ] Decide whether you will teach from the lesson page or require slides. If slides are required, produce decks only after each unit's sequence is signed off.
- [ ] Add one instructor-selected exemplar and one counterexample per unit. Keep answer logic private; publish student work only with permission.
- [ ] Time-box each B1/B2/B3 activity and note the cut point if the class runs late.
- [ ] Pin the tool/version assumptions used in demonstrations and record the expected fallback when an interface changes.
- [ ] Dry-run all export and hand-in packages on a clean student account, not only an instructor machine.
- [ ] Review the bilingual pair together after any substantive edit so EN and ES do not drift.

